# Summary
Introduced: a process-level information disclosure risk. The new issue-writing rule requires verbatim user text and the new issue demonstrates that format, but there is no carve-out for redacting webhook URLs, tokens, local paths, or other sensitive data before committing issue records.
AGENTS.md now instructs contributors/agents to write the user's original statement exactly as-is into issue files. In this project, user reports may naturally include sensitive values such as Discord webhook URLs, webhook tokens, local paths, QR-code URLs, logs, config snippets, or diagnostic excerpts. Because issue files are committed into the repository and moved under issues/closed, this creates a durable disclosure path for bearer secrets and private data. The rule should require preserving user intent while redacting or replacing secrets and privacy-sensitive values before committing.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Confirm the commit introduced a new requirement to record user statements verbatim in issue files.
- [x] Confirm issue files are repository-tracked artifacts and are moved into closed issue directories rather than treated as private transient notes.
- [x] Confirm the new rule and related scripts contain no explicit exception or sanitizer for webhook URLs, tokens, local paths, logs, QR URLs, or other private data.
- [x] Confirm the project context makes such sensitive values likely in user reports, especially Discord Webhook URLs/tokens and local diagnostic paths.
- [x] Demonstrate with a safe PoC that following the new rule preserves a fake webhook URL and local path verbatim in an issue markdown file.
## Report
Validated as a process/documentation-level information disclosure risk, not a runtime memory-safety bug. Dynamic crash/Valgrind/debugger validation is not applicable to the finding because the introduced behavior is an AGENTS.md workflow rule; the only changed executable script is an index-sort checker. I still ran the relevant script: `node scripts/check-closed-issue-index.mjs` returned `Closed issue index OK: 202 rows sorted`. `command -v valgrind` and `command -v gdb` returned nothing in the container, while `node` was present.

Evidence of introduction: parent commit AGENTS.md line 6 only required concise `問題`, `期待する挙動`, and `受け入れ条件`; current AGENTS.md:5-6 now requires creating/updating an issue before work and says the `指示` section must quote the user's statement `誤字も含めて原文のまま引用する` (verbatim including typos). AGENTS.md:8 then says completed tickets are moved into `issues/closed/...` and indexed, so these records are committed repository artifacts. The new issue file `issues/closed/unreleased/236-sort-closed-issue-index-and-preserve-user-instructions.md` is tracked and demonstrates the storage pattern: lines 3-22 place the raw user instruction in a fenced `text` block, and lines 40-45 accept that the new issue itself uses the new format.

Evidence the data can naturally be sensitive: README.md:130-145 explains users configure Discord Webhook URLs and explicitly warns that a Webhook URL can post and should not be shared. Existing closed security issues show the project already treats these values and local paths as sensitive: `issues/closed/v0.1.7/098-redact-diagnostic-secrets.md`:5-15 requires redacting Webhook URLs and Discord tokens from diagnostic data; `issues/closed/v0.1.7/102-redact-diagnostic-log-paths.md`:5-15 requires suppressing local user paths and Webhook/token values in logs. I checked the relevant workflow files/scripts and found no redaction carve-out or automation: `grep` over AGENTS/issues/docs showed no AGENTS.md rule for redacting secrets, and `grep -RIn --include='*.mjs' ... scripts` found only `scripts/check-closed-issue-index.mjs`, which validates sort order only.

PoC reproduction: I created a safe fake Discord-webhook-shaped URL and a fake Windows user path, then generated an issue markdown file following the new AGENTS.md rule. The PoC output showed exact persistence: `REPRODUCED: fake webhook URL and local path persisted verbatim in /workspace/validation_artifacts/clipforvrchat-verbatim-issue-poc/poc-output-issue.md`, with line 6 containing `webhookUrl=https://discord.com/api/webhooks/123456789012345678/FAKE_TOKEN_DO_NOT_USE_ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ` and line 7 containing `outputPath=C:\Users\alice\Pictures\VRChat\2026-07-07\secret-world.png`. This confirms that under the introduced rule, a user report containing a real bearer webhook URL/token or private path would be durably written to committed issue records unless the process adds an explicit redaction exception.

